Package: deconflate
Type: Package
Title: Comorbidity Adjustment of Disease Impact Estimates
Version: 0.5.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Philip", "Rasmussen", email = "phr@sund.ku.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Adjusts ("de-conflates") disease impact estimates for
    statistical associations between diseases, so that impacts can be
    aggregated without double counting (Rasmussen et al. 2022
    <doi:10.1016/j.prevetmed.2022.105617>). One model: a maximum-entropy
    distribution of disease combinations fitted to the disease
    prevalences and every association row (odds ratios, risk ratios, risk
    differences, phi, prevalences and odds ratio ratios, about pairs,
    combinations or subgroups, crude or adjusted), with pairs without an
    estimate filled in. Every impact row (crude, adjusted, within a
    subgroup, or about a combination of diseases) is an equation in each
    disease's own impact and the interactions; several estimates of one
    quantity are pooled or fitted together. Additive impacts (e.g. milk
    yield) and event impacts (hazard ratios, rate ratios, risk ratios,
    odds ratios and risk differences of, e.g., culling, through a snapshot
    hazard model with the risk attributable to disease) are supported.
    Includes Shapley attribution, propagation of input uncertainty, a
    diagnosis of conflicting inputs, feasibility checks, threshold
    searches and sensitivity screening.
